## Appendix B — Glossary / Glossario

- **AI Act** — Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and
  of the Council on artificial intelligence.
- **Annex III** — list of high-risk AI systems by category.
- **Annex IV** — required content of technical documentation for
  high-risk AI systems (the structure of this document).
- **GPAI** — General-Purpose AI model (Article 3(63)). Subject to
  separate obligations under Chapter V of the Act.
- **Provider** (Article 3(3)) — the natural or legal person that
  develops an AI system or has it developed and places it on the
  market or puts it into service under its own name or trademark.
- **Deployer** (Article 3(4)) — the natural or legal person using an
  AI system under its authority. Was previously called "user" in
  earlier drafts.
- **Authorised representative** (Article 3(5)) — required for
  non-EU-established providers (Article 22).
- **Conformity assessment** (Article 43) — the procedure
  demonstrating compliance for high-risk systems before market
  placement.
- **Post-market monitoring** (Article 72) — provider obligation to
  systematically collect and analyse data on system performance
  throughout its lifetime.
- **Article 5** — prohibited AI practices.
- **Article 6 + Annex III** — high-risk classification.
- **Article 9** — risk management system.
- **Article 12** — record-keeping (logs).
- **Article 13** — transparency and information for deployers.
- **Article 14** — human oversight.
- **Article 26** — deployer obligations for high-risk systems.
- **Article 27** — fundamental rights impact assessment.
- **Article 47** — EU declaration of conformity.
- **Article 50** — transparency obligations for certain AI systems.
- **Article 72** — post-market monitoring.
- **Article 73** — serious incident reporting.

